this one will just make private, so
we'll just say "void SetDifficulty()."

7
00:00:26.066 --> 00:00:27.966
Because I don't believe
we'll need this later,

8
00:00:27.966 --> 00:00:29.966
we'll just need it inside of this class.

9
00:00:30.433 --> 00:00:34.900
And then, for SetDifficulty(),
we're just going to test

10
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.833
and see if it works for now
using a "debug.log()" method,

11
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:42.400
so that way we can print
out to our console in Unity,

12
00:00:42.666 --> 00:00:48.700
and we're actually going
to get the "Button.gameObject.name,"

13
00:00:49.266 --> 00:00:51.733
so this will give
us the name of our Button.

14
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:57.133
Then we'll use a literal string,
to say, "was clicked,"

15
00:00:57.366 --> 00:00:59.866
so then when we press one
of the Buttons, for example,

16
00:00:59.866 --> 00:01:03.066
it should say Easy Button was clicked.

17
00:01:03.066 --> 00:01:05.566
And then, one thing we do
need to do, is we actually

18
00:01:05.566 --> 00:01:08.533
need to use this method
to see when a Button was clicked.

19
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.766
So, we can actually say Button.

20
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.133
Now, similar to what we had
with the Restart Button,

21
00:01:15.466 --> 00:01:19.233
where it had an "onClick()"
method, to Listen for when

22
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:21.500
the Button was clicked by the mouse,

23
00:01:21.866 --> 00:01:26.133
we can actually use that in code,
so we can actually use onClick,

24
00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:28.200
so when the Button is clicked,

25
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.533
we need our game to Listen,
to pay attention,

26
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:35.066
to when it's actually been clicked,
so in this case,

27
00:01:35.066 --> 00:01:37.533
